1:["$","main",null,{"id":"main","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"intro","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"intro-copy","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"MATHEMATICS & PROBABILITY · THEORY OF LEARNING & COMPUTATIONAL NEUROSCIENCE · QUANTUM INFORMATION & COMPUTATION"}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"Leo Flack"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"lead","children":"Using mathematics and computation to uncover emergent collective behaviour in physical and neural systems."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"affiliation","children":"University of Cambridge  /  École Polytechnique"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"links","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"#research","children":"Explore my research ↓"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/cv.html","children":"Read my CV →"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/documents/leo-flack-cv.pdf","download":"Resume Leo Flack.pdf","children":"Download CV · PDF ↓"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=XdcAmPsAAAAJ&hl=fr&oi=ao","children":"Google Scholar ↗"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/leoF333","children":"GitHub ↗"}]]}]]}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"portrait","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/leo-flack-portrait.jpg","alt":"Leo Flack","width":"390","height":"493"}]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"research","aria-labelledby":"research-title","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"research-title","className":"eyebrow","children":"SELECTED RESEARCH"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"2024 — 2026"}]]}],[["$","article","hopfield",{"className":"project","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"project-meta","children":["01"," / ","UNIVERSITY OF CHICAGO"," · ","March – August 2026"]}],["$","h2",null,{"children":["$","a",null,{"className":"project-title","href":"/research/hopfield.html","children":"In disordered neural networks, finite is different"}]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Hopfield networks are models of associative memory: they can hold a stored pattern fixed or, with delayed non-reciprocal interactions, replay patterns as a sequence. I study how the transition between these regimes changes from the thermodynamic limit to finite disordered networks, where memories destabilise one by one."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"tags","children":"Statistical Mechanics / Stability Analysis / DDE Integration"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"links","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/research/hopfield.html","children":"Read the project →"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/documents/hopfield-report.pdf","children":["Report"," ↗"]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"status-label","children":"Research internship · 2026"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"research-note","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"note-label","children":"THE CENTRAL QUESTION"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"How is sequential memory recall born from static pattern retrieval in associative memory neural networks?"}],["$","a",null,{"className":"note-foot","href":"https://github.com/leoF333/hopfield-dynamics","children":"EXPLORE THE CODE & DATA ↗"}]]}]]}],["$","article","learning",{"className":"project","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"project-meta","children":["02"," / ","ENS PARIS"," · ","September 2025 – March 2026"]}],["$","h2",null,{"children":["$","a",null,{"className":"project-title","href":"/research/learning.html","children":"Autoencoders and the statistical physics of high-dimensional learning"}]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"What determines whether an autoencoder learns a latent dynamics—or merely reconstructs its training set? Covariance spectra and replica theory connect the geometry of the data to generalisation."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"tags","children":"Statistical physics / Autoencoders / Replica theory"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"links","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/research/learning.html","children":"Read the project →"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"